  === Complete Solutions

  #sol-item(1, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    120 000 000 ÷ 600 000 = 200 people per km².
  ]

  #sol-item(2, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    A broad base means many births; a narrow apex means few survivors.
  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The narrow base shows that fewer children have been born in recent years.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Jobs and services draw; drought, land shortage and insecurity push.
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    A young population has many dependants for each worker.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Doubling time ≈ 70 ÷ 3.5 = 20 years.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    It is a change in the share of the population, not the size of one city.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    A broad base on the pyramid means a large child population.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    His claim was geometric population against arithmetic food.
  ]

  #sol-item(10, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The prefix marks the direction: ex out, in in.
  ]

  #sol-item(11, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Water is the first need and the first reason to stay.
  ]

  #sol-item(12, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    A shared centre produces the clustered, nucleated form.
  ]

  #sol-item(13, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Rent peaks where access peaks, and access peaks at the centre.
  ]

  #sol-item(14, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Merging urban areas produce a conurbation.
  ]

  #sol-item(15, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Range measures the journey; threshold measures the minimum demand.
  ]

  #sol-item(16, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Growth outruns housing, water, drains and transport.
  ]

  #sol-item(17, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Site is local; situation is regional.
  ]

  #sol-item(18, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The raised bank is the only buildable line, so the houses follow it.
  ]

  #sol-item(19, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Low inputs per hectare define the extensive system.
  ]

  #sol-item(20, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The tree needs humid heat, which limits it to the south.
  ]
  #pagebreak(weak: true)

  #sol-item(21, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    It tolerates a marked dry season and moderate rainfall.
  ]

  #sol-item(22, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    One crop means one price, and a fall in that price ruins the estate.
  ]

  #sol-item(23, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The herd must follow the grass and the wells.
  ]

  #sol-item(24, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Seed, water, advice and storage arrive separately, so each gain is small.
  ]

  #sol-item(25, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The regrowth returns the nutrients the crop removed.
  ]

  #sol-item(26, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Cocoa is grown for the world market; the others are mainly food crops.
  ]

  #sol-item(27, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
